                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d2529a40-c57e-40bb-a4c8-2049b20f74ce",
                        "entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "chiasmes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "cac11701-a8e1-4a96-8c6d-754816f4c95f",
                        "entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "chiasma"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e43d38d8-de0c-38e1-ba86-34dc51860d8c",
                        "entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rapprochement de deux constructions en miroir, suivant le schéma AB/BA afin de produire un effet de contraste ou de symétrie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rhetoric"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0699f83a-94cd-4fcb-9f42-44d8fb2f6b93",
                                "sense_id": "e43d38d8-de0c-38e1-ba86-34dc51860d8c",
                                "text": "La pièce de Jules Massenet est en effet tirée du roman éponyme d’Anatole France, à l’anticléricalisme revendiqué. La partition n’a pourtant gardé du synopsis que la double trajectoire telle un chiasme de deux destins aux mouvements contraires."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90782409-6916-4bf3-a10f-e046f54b187f",
                                "sense_id": "e43d38d8-de0c-38e1-ba86-34dc51860d8c",
                                "text": "Le chiasme est une figure très belle qui prouve que les Dupondt sont une créature de la syntaxe. On les prend pour des imbéciles notoires, mais en fait, ce sont des personnages qui ont recours à une syntaxe alambiquée et codée pour déjouer l’ennemi."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6480bf4f-2ad5-4674-ae6f-abb0114fa65c",
                                "sense_id": "e43d38d8-de0c-38e1-ba86-34dc51860d8c",
                                "text": "[…] mieux vaut une vérité de droite qu’une erreur de gauche. Ce chiasme du préférable n’est pas du cru d’Onfray. Note : Il ne s’agit pas ici d’un chiasme (forme ABBA) mais d’un parallélisme (forme ABAB)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e88aa83-b45d-41f7-94f2-3bc19ca4d25f",
                                "sense_id": "e43d38d8-de0c-38e1-ba86-34dc51860d8c",
                                "text": "Tristan Bernard jamais en reste :\nUn journal coupé en morceaux n’intéresse aucune femme, alors qu’une femme coupée en morceaux intéresse tous les journaux.\nUn joli chiasme (figure consistant à utiliser les mêmes mots mais en ordre inversé) […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3353ea61-a329-3927-9b14-1cdfcdcc8003",
                        "entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Croix mise en marge des manuscrits, en forme de χ, et indiquant un passage désapprouvé."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b479496e-250e-3737-b415-bce1e4cc8b33",
                        "entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lieu d’entrecroisement des nerfs optiques sur le corps de l’os sphénoïde."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eaf880b2-a0bf-4dd1-8b88-79000e1abd4f",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "source_sense_description": "figure rhétorique",
                        "target_lang_word": "Chiasmus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Chiasmus",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0bdcbfa-5bd0-36fb-8ad9-25cb342714af",
                                        "entry_id": "d8bec61d-951e-3ab8-8e0d-70aa433c1567",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "syntaktische Überkreuzstellung von Wörtern oder Satzteilen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Rhetorik"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ecdbe1a-fde3-42c3-ae2c-1f7c0996d471",
                                                "sense_id": "f0bdcbfa-5bd0-36fb-8ad9-25cb342714af",
                                                "text": "Ein Chiasmus entsteht, wenn zwei parallel gebaute Sätze ABC und ABC in der Form ABC und CBA wiedergegeben werden: Hier haust das Wiktionary, die Wikipedia haust dort."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1980199-ee7e-42cd-b3e9-0ce739839a93",
                                                "sense_id": "f0bdcbfa-5bd0-36fb-8ad9-25cb342714af",
                                                "text": "Ein bekannter Chiasmus aus Goethes Faust ist: „[…] die Kunst ist lang, / Und kurz ist unser Leben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5b3fb2d-a587-4b0a-8fe3-3dd811928c69",
                                                "sense_id": "f0bdcbfa-5bd0-36fb-8ad9-25cb342714af",
                                                "text": "„Eine Sonderform der Antithese ist der sogenannte Chiasmus (Kreuzstellung).“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "61ca6df4-614f-48a5-a44a-0947277326b7",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "source_sense_description": "figure rhétorique",
                        "target_lang_word": "chiasmus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chiasmus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                        "entry_id": "bf9adbac-1688-3ad6-a61c-48f6a2f88650",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An inversion of the relationship between the elements of phrases."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2ac3810-e3b5-4513-82c4-fc4011a3e39b",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "The book of Habakkuk has been discovered to consist of a closely knit chiastic structure throughout. This is the first poem of such length to stand revealed as a literary unit of this kind, though chiasmus has already been discovered throughout many psalms[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f532d064-458c-4b8e-bbe7-f5b4322d410c",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "John F. Kennedy is more famous for his chiasmus than for many of his policies:\n\"Ask not what your country can do for you—ask what you can do for your country.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7bd6203-4093-44b0-8fd2-3ea4716b0c9a",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "Leeman therefore holds that chiasmus is the basic order in Greek and Latin: antithesis is, he claims, normal for the modern, rational mind, but for the Greeks and Romans chiasmus was more natural."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1d3fabc-cc74-4c7d-857b-e0aaeeb7dc5c",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "The realization that Mawlānā was using parallelism and chiasmus to organize the higher levels of his work has been a major surprise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
