                                                "example_id": "b1d3fabc-cc74-4c7d-857b-e0aaeeb7dc5c",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "The realization that Mawlānā was using parallelism and chiasmus to organize the higher levels of his work has been a major surprise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "75854bb5-f542-47ae-8b34-32d8a84238c6",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "source_sense_description": "anatomie",
                        "target_lang_word": "Chiasma",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Chiasma",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7cad1cf8-b8ca-35de-9582-11ed2f57c0f4",
                                        "entry_id": "d7b8a171-a6d0-3fff-bbb0-a0165f059230",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Austausch von Segmenten zwischen zwei homologen Chromosomen während der Prophase I der Meiose"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Genetik",
                                            "Zytologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e48c88b-8ec1-409d-b53a-dc40df0cc84c",
                                                "sense_id": "7cad1cf8-b8ca-35de-9582-11ed2f57c0f4",
                                                "text": "F. A. JANSSENS beobachtete während der Meiose von Batrachoseps attenuatus (einem Amphibium) die Überkreuzung einzelner Chromosomenarme im Diplotänstadium und nannte diesen Zustand Chiasma."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8abde32f-f099-4d5a-a562-daecc24ad5e2",
                                                "sense_id": "7cad1cf8-b8ca-35de-9582-11ed2f57c0f4",
                                                "text": "\"Es liegt nahe, diese Chiasmata zu den aus Kreuzungsdaten erschlossenen Crossovern in Beziehung zu setzen … Diese Ergebnisse rechtfertigen die Auffassung, daß Crossover und Chiasmata verschiedene Aspekte des gleichen Phänomens sind …\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59b03e4a-2d6a-46a0-838c-b181020165d0",
                                                "sense_id": "7cad1cf8-b8ca-35de-9582-11ed2f57c0f4",
                                                "text": "Durch eine solche „Überkreuzung“ (Chiasma) werden die auf den abgetrennten Teilstücken liegenden Gene aus ihrer bisherigen Koppelungsgruppe gelöst und gegeneinander ausgetauscht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1faeb279-aca1-40aa-831a-1a9b8ec6419b",
                                                "sense_id": "7cad1cf8-b8ca-35de-9582-11ed2f57c0f4",
                                                "text": "Chiasma ist das lichtmikroskopische Erscheinungsbild eines Crossing-overs. Die beiden Begriffe werden oft synonym verwendet."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10769500-76dd-47e5-89ec-328a7efcc53b",
                        "source_entry_id": "c0af64dc-8501-35b7-8bae-661b559511dc",
                        "source_sense_description": "anatomie",
                        "target_lang_word": "chiasmus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chiasmus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                        "entry_id": "bf9adbac-1688-3ad6-a61c-48f6a2f88650",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An inversion of the relationship between the elements of phrases."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "rhetoric",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2ac3810-e3b5-4513-82c4-fc4011a3e39b",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "The book of Habakkuk has been discovered to consist of a closely knit chiastic structure throughout. This is the first poem of such length to stand revealed as a literary unit of this kind, though chiasmus has already been discovered throughout many psalms[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f532d064-458c-4b8e-bbe7-f5b4322d410c",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "John F. Kennedy is more famous for his chiasmus than for many of his policies:\n\"Ask not what your country can do for you—ask what you can do for your country.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7bd6203-4093-44b0-8fd2-3ea4716b0c9a",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "Leeman therefore holds that chiasmus is the basic order in Greek and Latin: antithesis is, he claims, normal for the modern, rational mind, but for the Greeks and Romans chiasmus was more natural."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1d3fabc-cc74-4c7d-857b-e0aaeeb7dc5c",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6903a9-5a07-3191-adf3-bf6c06e28d31",
                                                "text": "The realization that Mawlānā was using parallelism and chiasmus to organize the higher levels of his work has been a major surprise."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
